*> Implementation test (002-lane-mobs2, T4100; docs/protocol/18 section 7.5, 21 section 8.2, 17 section 4.10, 41 section 4): experience.
*> The level table (7 + 2 L, 37 + 5 (L - 15), 112 + 9 (L - 30)), the orb value tiers, giving points (levels, Set Experience 0x69), the
*> award split into orbs, merging (every 20th tick, ids 40 apart), the pickup (one orb per tick, takeXpDelay 2, Take Item Entity),
*> the pull toward a player within 8 blocks, gravity onto a floor and the 6000-tick lifetime.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-XP-ORBS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY RULES.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 65536.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(16) VALUE "Stefan".
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 6.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ENTITY-ROW          PIC X(66).
 01 WS-BLOCK               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BLOCK-ROW           PIC X(819).
 01 WS-STATE-TEXT          PIC X(5).
 01 WS-STONE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-AIR                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ORB-TYPE            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEVEL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NEEDED              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VALUE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TOTAL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-POINTS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SUM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VALUES              PIC X(40).
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-PADDED              PIC X(1030).
 01 WS-FOUND               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-BX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BY                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW-A               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW-B               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BEFORE              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DISTANCE            FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-TOTAL-AWARD         BINARY-LONG VALUE 100.
 01 WS-CAUSE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NONE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ONE-VALUE           BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-SEVEN               BINARY-LONG VALUE 7.
 01 WS-VALUE-EDIT          PIC -(9)9.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
*>   A world that is not standard has no orb type, and its tick does nothing.
     CALL "XP-ORB-TYPE" USING WS-ORB-TYPE
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "test xp: a world of the stand-in set has no orb type" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-ORB-TYPE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TEST-STANDARD-TABLES"
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "TEST-JOIN" USING WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-CONN
     MOVE CN-PLAYER(WS-CONN) TO WS-PLAYER
     MOVE PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-DIM
     MOVE "minecraft:experience_orb" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ORB-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE "minecraft:stone" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-BLOCK-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-BLOCK WS-BLOCK-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-BLOCK-ROW(1 + 4 + 35 + 32 + 288 + 4 + 5:5) TO WS-STATE-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-STONE = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-STATE-TEXT)
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE

*>   The level table.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LEVEL
     CALL "XP-NEEDED" USING WS-LEVEL WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "test xp: level 0 needs 7 points" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 7 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 14 TO WS-LEVEL
     CALL "XP-NEEDED" USING WS-LEVEL WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "test xp: level 14 needs 35 points" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 35 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 15 TO WS-LEVEL
     CALL "XP-NEEDED" USING WS-LEVEL WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "test xp: level 15 needs 37 points" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 37 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 29 TO WS-LEVEL
     CALL "XP-NEEDED" USING WS-LEVEL WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "test xp: level 29 needs 107 points" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 107 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 30 TO WS-LEVEL
     CALL "XP-NEEDED" USING WS-LEVEL WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "test xp: level 30 needs 112 points" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 112 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 31 TO WS-LEVEL
     CALL "XP-NEEDED" USING WS-LEVEL WS-NEEDED
     MOVE "test xp: level 31 needs 121 points" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 121 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-NEEDED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The orb value tiers (21 section 8.2).
     MOVE 100 TO WS-TOTAL
     CALL "XP-ORB-VALUE" USING WS-TOTAL WS-VALUE
     MOVE "test xp: an award of 100 starts with an orb of 73" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 73 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-VALUE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 2 TO WS-TOTAL
     CALL "XP-ORB-VALUE" USING WS-TOTAL WS-VALUE
     MOVE "test xp: an award of 2 is an orb of 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-VALUE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 99999 TO WS-TOTAL
     CALL "XP-ORB-VALUE" USING WS-TOTAL WS-VALUE
     MOVE "test xp: the largest orb is 2477" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2477 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-VALUE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Giving points: levels, progress and Set Experience (0x69).
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     MOVE 7 TO WS-POINTS
     CALL "XP-GIVE" USING WS-PLAYER WS-POINTS
     MOVE "test xp: 7 points make level 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-LEVEL(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: the progress of the level restarts at 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-POINTS(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     PERFORM FIND-105
     MOVE "test xp: Set Experience (105) was sent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-FOUND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 8 TO WS-POINTS
     CALL "XP-GIVE" USING WS-PLAYER WS-POINTS
     MOVE "test xp: 8 more points stay in level 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 8 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-POINTS(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: the total counts every point" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 15 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 202 TO WS-POINTS
     CALL "XP-GIVE" USING WS-PLAYER WS-POINTS
     MOVE "test xp: 217 points in all are level 12" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 12 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-LEVEL(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: and 1 point into it" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-POINTS(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The total stops at the int range.
     MOVE 2147483647 TO WS-POINTS
     CALL "XP-GIVE" USING WS-PLAYER WS-POINTS
     MOVE "test xp: the total is capped at 2147483647" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2147483647 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PL-XP-LEVEL(WS-PLAYER) PL-XP-POINTS(WS-PLAYER) PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER)

*>   A floor and room for the orb tests beside the player.
     COMPUTE WS-BX = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-X(WS-PLAYER)) + 12
     COMPUTE WS-BY = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Y(WS-PLAYER)) + 20
     COMPUTE WS-BZ = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Z(WS-PLAYER))
     CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-BX WS-BY WS-BZ WS-STONE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 8
         COMPUTE WS-N = WS-BY + WS-I
         CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-BX WS-N WS-BZ WS-AIR
     END-PERFORM

*>   The award splits 100 into 73, 17, 7 and 3 (E7), at the position.
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-BX + 0.5
     COMPUTE WS-Y = WS-BY + 3
     COMPUTE WS-Z = WS-BZ + 0.5
     CALL "XP-AWARD" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-TOTAL-AWARD
     PERFORM LIST-ORBS
     MOVE "test xp: an award of 100 makes four orbs" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 4 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-N TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: of 73, 17, 7 and 3" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "73,17,7,3" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-VALUES TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     PERFORM CLEAR-ORBS
*>   Small awards at one spot merge into a near orb when its id fits the draw: the points are all kept in fewer orbs.
     PERFORM 300 TIMES
         MOVE 1 TO WS-POINTS
         CALL "XP-AWARD" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-POINTS
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM LIST-ORBS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SUM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > EN-COUNT
         IF EN-USED(WS-I) = 1 AND EN-TYPE(WS-I) = WS-ORB-TYPE
             ADD EN-ITEM-COUNT(WS-I) TO WS-SUM
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "test xp: 300 single points are 300 pieces" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 300 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: some of the pieces merged into a near orb" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-N < 300
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM CLEAR-ORBS

*>   Merging on the first tick: two orbs of one value, ids 40 apart, within half a block.
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-ONE-VALUE WS-ROW-A
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-ONE-VALUE WS-ROW-B
     COMPUTE EN-ID(WS-ROW-B) = EN-ID(WS-ROW-A) + 40
     MOVE 10 TO EN-AGE(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE 3 TO EN-AGE(WS-ROW-B)
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     PERFORM LIST-ORBS
     MOVE "test xp: two orbs 40 ids apart merge into one" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-N TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: the survivor represents both" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-ITEM-COUNT(WS-ROW-A) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: the merged orb keeps the smaller age (3, plus the tick)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 4 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-AGE(WS-ROW-A) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM CLEAR-ORBS
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-ONE-VALUE WS-ROW-A
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-ONE-VALUE WS-ROW-B
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     PERFORM LIST-ORBS
     MOVE "test xp: orbs with neighbouring ids do not merge" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-N TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM CLEAR-ORBS

*>   Gravity: the orb falls onto the floor and rests on it.
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-ONE-VALUE WS-ROW-A
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VX(WS-ROW-A) EN-VZ(WS-ROW-A)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 80
         CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-DISTANCE = EN-Y(WS-ROW-A) - (WS-BY + 1)
     MOVE "test xp: the orb comes to rest on the floor" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-USED(WS-ROW-A) = 1 AND FUNCTION ABS(WS-DISTANCE) < 0.02 AND EN-ON-GROUND(WS-ROW-A) = 1
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Lifetime: at age 6000 the orb is gone.
     MOVE 5999 TO EN-AGE(WS-ROW-A)
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     MOVE "test xp: an orb of age 6000 is discarded" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USED(WS-ROW-A) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Walls and a ceiling on the platform: a solid cell ahead cancels that horizontal motion; one above stops a rise.
     COMPUTE WS-BX = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-X(WS-PLAYER)) + 12
     COMPUTE WS-BY = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Y(WS-PLAYER)) + 20
     COMPUTE WS-BZ = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Z(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-N = WS-BX + 1
     COMPUTE WS-I = WS-BY + 1
     CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-N WS-I WS-BZ WS-STONE
     COMPUTE WS-N = WS-BZ + 1
     CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-BX WS-I WS-N WS-STONE
     COMPUTE WS-I = WS-BY + 3
     CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-BX WS-I WS-BZ WS-STONE
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-BX + 0.5
     COMPUTE WS-Y = WS-BY + 1
     COMPUTE WS-Z = WS-BZ + 0.5
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-ONE-VALUE WS-ROW-A
     MOVE 0.6 TO EN-VX(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VZ(WS-ROW-A) EN-VY(WS-ROW-A)
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     MOVE "test xp: a wall ahead on x stops the orb" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(EN-X(WS-ROW-A) - WS-X) < 0.001
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VX(WS-ROW-A) EN-VY(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE 0.6 TO EN-VZ(WS-ROW-A)
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     MOVE "test xp: a wall ahead on z stops the orb" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(EN-Z(WS-ROW-A) - WS-Z) < 0.001
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     COMPUTE EN-Y(WS-ROW-A) = WS-BY + 2.2
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VX(WS-ROW-A) EN-VZ(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE 0.5 TO EN-VY(WS-ROW-A)
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     COMPUTE WS-DISTANCE = EN-Y(WS-ROW-A) - (WS-BY + 2.2)
     MOVE "test xp: a ceiling above stops the orb rising" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-DISTANCE) < 0.001
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM CLEAR-ORBS

*>   Room and floor beside the player for the pull and the pickup.
     COMPUTE WS-BX = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-X(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-BY = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Y(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-BZ = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Z(WS-PLAYER))
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 2 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 6
         COMPUTE WS-N = WS-BX + WS-I
         COMPUTE WS-BY = WS-BY - 1
         CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-N WS-BY WS-BZ WS-STONE
         COMPUTE WS-BY = WS-BY + 1
         CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-N WS-BY WS-BZ WS-AIR
         COMPUTE WS-BY = WS-BY + 1
         CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-N WS-BY WS-BZ WS-AIR
         COMPUTE WS-BY = WS-BY - 1
     END-PERFORM
*>   The pull: an orb 4 blocks away moves toward the player, and is not yet picked up after 5 ticks.
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-BX + 4.5
     MOVE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Y
     COMPUTE WS-Z = WS-BZ + 0.5
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-ONE-VALUE WS-ROW-A
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VX(WS-ROW-A) EN-VZ(WS-ROW-A) EN-VY(WS-ROW-A)
     COMPUTE WS-DISTANCE = FUNCTION ABS(EN-X(WS-ROW-A) - PL-X(WS-PLAYER))
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 5
         CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "test xp: an orb within 8 blocks is pulled toward the player" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-USED(WS-ROW-A) = 1 AND FUNCTION ABS(EN-X(WS-ROW-A) - PL-X(WS-PLAYER)) < WS-DISTANCE - 0.02
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM CLEAR-ORBS

*>   Pickup: one orb a tick, then the delay of 2 ticks; the player gets the value, the viewers Take Item Entity.
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     MOVE PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-BEFORE
     MOVE PL-X(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-X
     MOVE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Y
     MOVE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Z
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-SEVEN WS-ROW-A
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-SEVEN WS-ROW-B
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     COMPUTE WS-SUM = PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) - WS-BEFORE
     MOVE "test xp: the first tick picks up one orb of 7" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 7 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     COMPUTE WS-SUM = PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) - WS-BEFORE
     MOVE "test xp: the second tick picks up nothing (takeXpDelay)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 7 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     COMPUTE WS-SUM = PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) - WS-BEFORE
     MOVE "test xp: the third tick picks up the other" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 14 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FOUND
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING WS-FOUND FOR ALL "127"
     MOVE "test xp: the viewers got Take Item Entity (127)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-FOUND > 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM LIST-ORBS
     MOVE "test xp: both orbs are gone" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-N TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   An orb of count 3 is picked up three times (count - 1 each time).
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-SEVEN WS-ROW-A
     MOVE 3 TO EN-ITEM-COUNT(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-BEFORE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 7
         CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-SUM = PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) - WS-BEFORE
     MOVE "test xp: an orb of count 3 gives its value three times" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 21 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A dead player picks up nothing.
     CALL "XP-ORB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-SEVEN WS-ROW-A
     MOVE PL-X(WS-PLAYER) TO EN-X(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) TO EN-Y(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) TO EN-Z(WS-ROW-A)
     MOVE PS-DEAD TO PL-STATE(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-BEFORE
     CALL "XP-ORBS-TICK"
     MOVE "test xp: a dead player picks up no orb" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-BEFORE TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE PS-ALIVE TO PL-STATE(WS-PLAYER)
*>   Death: min(level x 7, 100) points drop as orbs at the player and the experience is reset (17 section 4.10).
     PERFORM CLEAR-ORBS
     MOVE 12 TO PL-XP-LEVEL(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 5 TO PL-XP-POINTS(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 300 TO PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 6 TO WS-CAUSE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-NONE
     CALL "HEALTH-DIE" USING WS-PLAYER WS-CAUSE WS-NONE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SUM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > EN-COUNT
         IF EN-USED(WS-I) = 1 AND EN-TYPE(WS-I) = WS-ORB-TYPE
             COMPUTE WS-SUM = WS-SUM + EN-ITEM(WS-I) * EN-ITEM-COUNT(WS-I)
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "test xp: a player of level 12 drops 84 points of orbs at death" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 84 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "test xp: and starts again at level 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = PL-XP-LEVEL(WS-PLAYER) + PL-XP-TOTAL(WS-PLAYER) + PL-XP-POINTS(WS-PLAYER)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     STOP RUN.
 LIST-ORBS.
*>   WS-N orbs in the tracker, WS-VALUES their values in id order, comma separated.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-VALUES
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > EN-COUNT
         IF EN-USED(WS-I) = 1 AND EN-TYPE(WS-I) = WS-ORB-TYPE
             ADD 1 TO WS-N
             MOVE EN-ITEM(WS-I) TO WS-VALUE-EDIT
             IF WS-N = 1
                 MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-VALUE-EDIT) TO WS-VALUES
             ELSE
                 STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-VALUES) "," FUNCTION TRIM(WS-VALUE-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-VALUES
             END-IF
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM.
 CLEAR-ORBS.
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > EN-COUNT
         IF EN-USED(WS-I) = 1 AND EN-TYPE(WS-I) = WS-ORB-TYPE
             CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-I
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM.
 FIND-105.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PADDED
     STRING " " DELIMITED BY SIZE WS-TEXT DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-PADDED
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FOUND
     INSPECT WS-PADDED TALLYING WS-FOUND FOR ALL " 105"
     IF WS-FOUND > 0
         MOVE 1 TO WS-FOUND
     END-IF.
 END PROGRAM TEST-XP-ORBS.
 COPY CORETEST.
